The following files are required for this assignment:
- FiniteFunctions.h
- FiniteFunctions.cxx
- CustomDistributions.h
- CustomDistributions.cxx
- CalculatePi.cxx
- MysteryData23232.txt
- Makefile

For the first part you will need to run 'make'. Then you will need to run ./CustomDistributions in the terminal.
This will produce three graphs, one being the function I believe is the one closest to the mystery data. This graph
will have the Metropolis algorthim applied to it.

For the bonus part, you will need to run 'make CalculatePi'. Then run ./CalculatePi [radius] [number of Metropolis samples]
and you will get a calculation of pi based on the inputs you provided.

I have also included the MysteryData23232.txt as I did not know whether or not you would need to generate it.

